\documentclass{article}
\title{Sample Complexity of Kernel Ridge Regression}
\author{F. Ilves and C. Marlowe}
\date{April 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Setting}
Let the covariates take values in $\mathbb{R}^d$ with uniformly bounded norm.
The excess risk of the ridge estimator decays at a rate governed by the effective
dimension of the kernel at the chosen regularisation level.
Our upper bound matches the minimax lower bound up to logarithmic factors,
and it recovers the classical parametric rate for finite dimensional kernels.
\end{document}

